---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import YouTubeEmbed from '../components/YouTubeEmbed.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import corgiRed from '../assets/dogs/corgi-red.webp';
import shepherdMix from '../assets/dogs/shepherd-mix.webp';
import corgiTri from '../assets/dogs/corgi-tri.webp';
import threeDogs from '../assets/dogs/three-dogs.webp';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.webp';

const dogs = [
  { src: corgiRed, alt: 'A red and white corgi looking up at the camera' },
  { src: shepherdMix, alt: 'A tan and black mixed-breed dog sitting on a couch' },
  { src: corgiTri, alt: 'A black, white and tan corgi resting on the back of a couch' },
  { src: threeDogs, alt: 'Three dogs lined up along the back of a couch' },
];

const linkedinLabel = site.linkedin.replace(/^https?:\/\/(www\.)?/, '').replace(/\/$/, '');

const currently = [
  {
    what: 'Principal Machine Learning Researcher',
    where: 'Analytical Mechanics Associates (NASA)',
    detail:
      'Researching agentic processes for GIS automation with the Center for Earth Observation Sciences: urbanization, burn scars, environmental change from satellite spectra.',
    href: '/published',
  },
];

const sections = [
  {
    href: '/experience',
    label: 'Experience',
    blurb:
      'Natural language processing, medical and pharmaceutical prior authorizations, automated medical billing and coding, agentic AI, and engineering leadership.',
  },
  {
    href: '/code',
    label: 'Code',
    blurb:
      'My public GitHub, demonstrating quantization, my machine learning library, fragile-token detector, and other machine learning related projects.',
  },
  {
    href: '/published',
    label: 'Published Work',
    blurb:
      'Research on fragile tokens, automated earth observation, best practices for agentic AI, and YouTube tutorials.',
  },
  {
    href: '/interests',
    label: 'Interests',
    blurb:
      'Undertrained tokens, inference cost, plasma dynamics, racing, and the teaching and volunteer work I give time to.',
  },
  {
    href: '/tutorials',
    label: 'Tutorials',
    blurb:
      'A free website for learning machine learning from core principles, with interactive playgrounds computed by my own library.',
  },
];
---

<Base>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-photo">
      <Image
        src={headshot}
        alt="Jeffrey Gordon"
        widths={[160, 320]}
        sizes="7.5rem"
        loading="eager"
      />
    </div>
    <div>
      <h1>Jeffrey Gordon</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">{site.tagline} - {site.location}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Section label="My Professional Side">
    <div class="intro prose">
      <p>
        My name is Jeffrey Gordon. I am an AI and machine learning expert with
        twenty years of experience, specializing in natural language processing.
      </p>
      <p>
        My experience ranges from early rule engines, taxonomies, ontologies, and
        knowledge graphs to the latest language models. I have focused
        extensively on healthcare and governance, risk, and compliance.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the past ten years, I have discovered my passion for technical-based
        leadership, taking a people-first approach to inspire teams through
        collaboration and software engineering mentorship. The teams I have led
        consistently meet objectives and exceed KPIs. An outcome I attribute to
        this close collaboration, regular feedback, and strong cross-team
        communication with leadership.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside applied AI expertise, I have a deep understanding of the
        foundational mechanisms of modern AI systems. My open-source
        contributions include implementing GPTQ 4-bit NormalFloat quantization,
        LoRA and QLoRA fine-tuning, and developing techniques to analyze
        transformer architectures. My recent research examines hallucination
        mechanisms and their relationship to fragile tokens. I also support
        learning in machine learning and AI through a free tutorial website, a
        YouTube channel, and a Discord community of 75,000 members.
      </p>
      <p>
        In my work with Agentic AI systems, I place particular emphasis on
        deterministic guards, MCPs, tool contracts that define the agent's
        sandbox, and human-in-the-loop feedback. Much of my work focuses on voice
        applications where agents interact with customers and automated software
        development pipelines. I believe this makes evaluation and observability
        not only essential but required. I design pipelines linking containment,
        latency, and agent quality to business KPIs. This work has driven my
        research in agentic safety because critical failure modes often don't
        appear in standard demonstrations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="My Personal Side">
    <div class="intro prose">
      <p>
        When I'm not at my computer, I'm racing. I have an SCCA license and spend
        most weekends at the track or prepping a car. Currently, I am building a
        NASA-compliant Type-65 Coupe-R replica from Factory Five Racing. While,
        yes, originally a Ford, I am blasphemously mounting an LSX motor mated to
        a dual-clutch paddle-shift transmission.
      </p>
      <YouTubeEmbed
        id="t4Vno6aQIzU"
        poster="/media/vette-run.webp"
        label="In-car footage of a lap on track, with a telemetry overlay"
      />
      <p>
        I also race in simulators and am currently ranked in the top 100 for both
        Gran Turismo 7 and Assetto Corsa Competizione. While nothing beats real
        seat time, it is certainly far less expensive than tires and brakes. It
        also offers a great way to learn a track before actually racing on it.
      </p>
      <YouTubeEmbed
        id="PCQOkjzujn0"
        poster="/media/gt7-lap.webp"
        label="A cockpit-view lap in Gran Turismo 7"
      />
      <p>
        I began in mechanical engineering, hoping to build race cars, with a
        particular interest in aerodynamics. If your car can't stick the ground,
        it doesn't matter how much power it can generate. Outside of racing, I
        spend time learning computational physics, most recently plasma
        dynamics; it's more interesting than it sounds.
      </p>
      <p>
        I love dogs and have been involved in dog rescue for most of my life, and
        my own dogs came to me as rescues too. If you ever visit, expect to be
        greeted by several of them, most likely from the back of the couch.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="dogs" aria-label="Photos of my dogs">
      {
        dogs.map((d) => (
          <li>
            <Image
              src={d.src}
              alt={d.alt}
              widths={[320, 640]}
              sizes="(min-width: 52rem) 12rem, 55vw"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Currently">
    <ul class="currently">
      {
        currently.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <p class="c-what">
              {c.what}
              <span class="c-where">{c.where}</span>
            </p>
            <p class="c-detail">{c.detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Elsewhere">
    <ul class="sections">
      {
        sections.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <a
              href={s.href}
              target={s.external ? '_blank' : undefined}
              rel={s.external ? 'noopener' : undefined}
            >
              <span class="s-label">
                {s.label}
                <span class="s-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                  {s.external ? '↗' : '→'}
                </span>
              </span>
              <span class="s-blurb">{s.blurb}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Contact">
    <p class="prose">The fastest way to reach me is email.</p>
    <ul class="contact-links">
      <li>
        <span class="c-key">Email</span>
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="c-key">LinkedIn</span>
        <a href={site.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{linkedinLabel}</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="c-key">GitHub</span>
        <a href={`https://github.com/${site.github}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          github.com/{site.github}
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="c-key">YouTube</span>
        <a href={site.youtube.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          youtube.com/@{site.youtube.handle}
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>
</Base>


<style>
  .hero {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .hero-photo {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: clamp(5.25rem, 18vw, 7.5rem);
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--paper-sunk);
  }

  .hero-photo :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .hero h1 { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }

  .hero-sub {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono-stack);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .intro p { color: var(--ink-soft); }

  /* ---- Currently -------------------------------------------------------- */

  .currently {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .currently li {
    margin: 0;
    padding-block: 1.05rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .currently li:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: 0; }

  .c-what {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
  }

  .c-where {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-stack);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .c-detail {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62ch;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* ---- Elsewhere -------------------------------------------------------- */

  .sections {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .sections li {
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .sections li:first-child { border-top: 0; }

  .sections a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem 2rem;
    padding-block: 1rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .s-label {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .s-arrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-left: 0.4rem;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }

  .sections a:hover .s-label { color: var(--accent-hover); }
  .sections a:hover .s-arrow { transform: translateX(3px); }

  .s-blurb {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  @media (min-width: 46rem) {
    .sections a { grid-template-columns: 11rem minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: baseline; }
  }

  /* One row, never a grid. On narrow screens the row scrolls sideways
     rather than wrapping into a 2 x 2 block. */
  .dogs {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 0 0 0.25rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
  }

  .dogs li {
    margin: 0;
    flex: 0 0 55%;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }

  .dogs img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--paper-sunk);
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .dogs { overflow-x: visible; }
    .dogs li { flex: 1 1 0; }
  }

  .contact-links {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.35rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }

  .contact-links li {
    margin: 0;
    padding-block: 0.6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.1rem 1rem;
  }

  .contact-links li:first-child { border-top: 0; }

  .c-key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono-stack);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .contact-links a {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (min-width: 30rem) {
    .contact-links li {
      grid-template-columns: 6rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: baseline;
    }
  }
</style>
